{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0098025","isObsolete":false,"name":"virus tail, baseplate","definition":{"text":"Multiprotein component at the distal (head) end of the virus tail to which fibers of tailed viruses may be attached.","xrefs":[{"dbCode":"VZ","dbId":"3957"}]},"comment":"Tail fibers are often attached to the baseplate of Caudovirales (tailed bacteriophages with dsDNA genomes). Sometimes referred to as the tail tip or tip structure in Siphoviridae.","synonyms":[{"name":"bacteriophage baseplate","type":"narrow"},{"name":"tail structure","type":"related"},{"name":"tail tip","type":"related"}],"history":[{"timestamp":"2024-09-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2023-12-26","action":"Added","category":"XREF","text":"VZ:3957"},{"timestamp":"2012-08-09","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"Multiprotein component at the distal (head) end of the virus tail to which fibers of tailed viruses may be attached."},{"timestamp":"2012-08-09","action":"Added","category":"TERM","text":"virus tail, baseplate"},{"timestamp":"2012-08-09","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"part of GO:0098015 (virus tail)"},{"timestamp":"2012-08-09","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044423 (virion component)"},{"timestamp":"2012-08-09","action":"Added","category":"SYNONYM","text":"tail tip"},{"timestamp":"2012-08-09","action":"Added","category":"SYNONYM","text":"bacteriophage baseplate"},{"timestamp":"2012-08-09","action":"Added","category":"SYNONYM","text":"tail structure"}],"xRefs":[{"dbCode":"UniProtKB-KW","dbId":"KW-1226","name":"Viral baseplate protein"},{"dbCode":"VZ","dbId":"3957"}],"taxonConstraints":[{"ancestorId":"GO:0098025","ancestorName":"virus tail, baseplate","relationship":"never_in_taxon","taxId":"131567","taxIdType":"NCBITaxon","taxName":"cellular organisms"}],"aspect":"cellular_component","usage":"Unrestricted"}],"pageInfo":null}